    preview: "AfD celebrate projected win in Saxony-Anhalt Germany's far-right Alternative für Deutschland (AfD) is celebrating as exit polls show they are set to win more than 44% of the vote in the eastern state of Saxony-Anhalt. The AfD's projected result is higher than earlier opinion polls suggested and the party has hailed the news as a \"historic outcome\". However, party leaders will not know if they have enough seats to govern until they see which of the smaller parties get into the state parliament.",
    body: "AfD celebrate projected win in Saxony-Anhalt\n\nGermany's far-right Alternative für Deutschland (AfD) is celebrating as exit polls show they are set to win more than 44% of the vote in the eastern state of Saxony-Anhalt.\n\nThe AfD's projected result is higher than earlier opinion polls suggested and the party has hailed the news as a \"historic outcome\".\n\nHowever, party leaders will not know if they have enough seats to govern until they see which of the smaller parties get into the state parliament.\n\nThat may hinge on whether one of the smaller parties gets over the required threshold of 5%.\n\nBerlin correspondent Jess Parker reports from the AfD party HQ as supporters celebrated the projected results.\n\nRelated topics\n\n- Alternative for Germany (AfD)Updates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- GermanyUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.",
